    "title": "pandas.CategoricalIndex.as_unordered — pandas 2.2.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.CategoricalIndex.as_unordered#\n\n- \nCategoricalIndex.as_unordered(**args* ,***kwargs* )[source]#\n- Set the Categorical to be unordered. \n  - Returns:\n    - Categorical\n    - Unordered Categorical.\n Examples For `pandas.Series` :>>> raw_cat = pd.Categorical(['a', 'b', 'c', 'a'], ordered=True) >>> ser = pd.Series(raw_cat) >>> ser.cat.ordered True >>> ser = ser.cat.as_unordered() >>> ser.cat.ordered False For `pandas.CategoricalIndex` :>>> ci = pd.CategoricalIndex(['a', 'b', 'c', 'a'], ordered=True) >>> ci.ordered True >>> ci = ci.as_unordered() >>> ci.ordered False",
